ClearSkies — Privacy Policy
Last updated: August 14, 2026

ClearSkies is a browser extension that highlights corporate jargon on web pages and lets you rewrite your own text into exaggerated corporate phrasing, for readability and entertainment purposes.

What ClearSkies accesses
ClearSkies reads the visible text of the pages you view, solely to match it against a jargon dictionary bundled with the extension (used by Decode and Turbulence modes). When you use Corporate-ify, it reads the text you've selected or pasted into the popup.

What ClearSkies does not do
Does not collect, store, or transmit your browsing history or page content to any server
Does not track clicks, keystrokes, mouse movement, or any other user activity
Does not sell or share any data with third parties
Makes no network requests from its content script — all jargon matching happens locally in your browser
What ClearSkies stores
The extension stores one small preference locally on your device using chrome.storage.local: your selected mode (Off, Decode, or Turbulence). This never leaves your device and is not linked to any personal identifier.

Changes to this policy
If ClearSkies adds features that change what data it accesses (for example, an optional AI-powered rewrite mode that sends selected text to an external API), this page will be updated first, and the change will be reflected in the extension's permissions and store listing.

Contact
Questions about this policy can be sent via the extension's Chrome Web Store support page or GitHub repository.

ClearSkies is an independent, non-commercial project.
